{#-
  Renders the "## Execution graph" section, plus "## State" when the playbook declares
  state machines. Inputs:
    graph        — dict[str, list[str]] outer node → deps, insertion order preserved
    waves        — list[list[str]] resolved outer wave order (parallel members per wave)
    subgraphs    — dict[str, SubgraphNode] outer keys that are subgraph nodes
    inner_waves  — dict[str, list[list[str]]] resolved wave order per subgraph
    playbook     — the playbook name (for the state command invocations)
    states       — list of state entries from render_playbook._state_entries (may be empty)
  Emits a mermaid flowchart (one `subgraph … end` cluster per subgraph node, one edge
  line per dep, isolated nodes as bare ids) followed by a numbered wave list
  ("∥"-joined members share a wave; a subgraph's inner waves nest under its entry).
-#}
